  "answer": "Fixed the generic inference bug by changing the parameter types from `EndpointCandidate` to `T` so that TypeScript infers `T` from the actual `candidates` array and the `predicate` receives the inferred subtype, instead of widening to the base `EndpointCandidate` constraint.

Source patch hunk:

```diff
--- a/src/evaluateEligibility.ts
+++ b/src/evaluateEligibility.ts
@@ -10,9 +10,9 @@ function evaluateEligibility<T extends EndpointCandidate>(
-  candidates: EndpointCandidate[],
-  predicate: (candidate: EndpointCandidate) => boolean
+  candidates: T[],
+  predicate: (candidate: T) => boolean
 ): EligibilityResult<T>[] {
   return candidates.map(candidate => ({
     candidate,
     eligible: predicate(candidate),
   }));
 }
```

Updated unit tests:

```typescript
// src/evaluateEligibility.test.ts
import { evaluateEligibility } from './evaluateEligibility';

interface EndpointCandidate {
  id: string;
  score: number;
}

interface PremiumEndpointCandidate extends EndpointCandidate {
  tier: 'premium';
}

describe('evaluateEligibility', () => {
  it('infers the specific candidate subtype from the candidates array', () => {
    const candidates: PremiumEndpointCandidate[] = [
      { id: '1', score: 85, tier: 'premium' },
      { id: '2', score: 60, tier: 'premium' },
    ];

    const results = evaluateEligibility(
      candidates,
      (candidate) => candidate.score >= 70,
    );

    // This assignment only type-checks if T is inferred as PremiumEndpointCandidate
    const first: PremiumEndpointCandidate = results[0].candidate;
    expect(first.tier).toBe('premium');
    expect(results[0].eligible).toBe(true);
    expect(results[1].eligible).toBe(false);
  });

  it('predicate receives the inferred subtype, not the base type', () => {
    const candidates: PremiumEndpointCandidate[] = [
      { id: '1', score: 85, tier: 'premium' },
    ];

    evaluateEligibility(candidates, (candidate) => {
      // Compile-time assertion: `tier` is accessible only on PremiumEndpointCandidate
      return candidate.tier === 'premium' && candidate.score >= 70;
    });
  });
});
```"
}

